\b SabCargo API to SQL Server Setup Guide\b0\par
\par
This guide explains how to connect your SabCargo backend API to Microsoft SQL Server in a clear step-by-step flow.\par
Each step includes a short introduction so you understand why it is needed.\par
\par
\b Step 1: Confirm Required Software\b0\par
Before setup, make sure required tools are installed.\par
- SQL Server\par
- SSMS\par
- Node.js and npm\par
- Flutter SDK\par
\par
\b Step 2: Create SQL Login and Database User\b0\par
The backend API needs a SQL login with database permissions.\par
Run this in SSMS New Query:\par
{\f1
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.server_principals WHERE name = 'sabcargo_app')\par
BEGIN\par
    CREATE LOGIN sabcargo_app WITH PASSWORD = 'Pakistan@123';\par
END\par
ELSE\par
BEGIN\par
    ALTER LOGIN sabcargo_app WITH PASSWORD = 'Pakistan@123';\par
END\par
GO\par
\par
USE SabCargoDB;\par
GO\par
\par
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.database_principals WHERE name = 'sabcargo_app')\par
BEGIN\par
    CREATE USER sabcargo_app FOR LOGIN sabcargo_app;\par
END\par
GO\par
\par
ALTER ROLE db_owner ADD MEMBER sabcargo_app;\par
GO\par
}\par
\b Step 3: Enable Mixed Mode\b0\par
In SSMS server Properties > Security, choose SQL Server and Windows Authentication mode, then restart SQL Server service.\par
\par
\b Step 4: Configure Backend .env\b0\par
Create file backend/.env with:\par
{\f1
PORT=5000\par
DB_USER=sabcargo_app\par
DB_PASSWORD=Pakistan@123\par
DB_SERVER=DESKTOP-OPPHQ49\par
DB_PORT=1433\par
DB_NAME=SabCargoDB\par
}\par
\b Step 5: Install Dependencies\b0\par
{\f1 cd "C:\\Users\\hp\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\sabcargo\\backend"\par
npm.cmd install\par
}\par
\b Step 6: Start Backend API\b0\par
{\f1 npm.cmd start\par
}\par
Expected logs:\par
- Server running on http://localhost:5000\par
- Connected to SQL Server\par
\par
If port 5000 is busy:\par
{\f1 taskkill /F /IM node.exe\par
npm.cmd start\par
}\par
\b Step 7: Platform API URLs\b0\par
- Web: http://localhost:5000/api\par
- Android emulator: http://10.0.2.2:5000/api\par
- Windows desktop: http://localhost:5000/api\par
\par
\b Step 8: Run Flutter App\b0\par
In second terminal:\par
{\f1
cd "C:\\Users\\hp\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\sabcargo"\par
flutter run\par
}\par
\b Step 9: Verify API\b0\par
Open: http://localhost:5000/api/users\par
If JSON appears, API-to-SQL connection is working.\par
\par
\b Daily Quick Run\b0\par
